WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:13.220
I'm Doe Deer.

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:17.235
I have a channel on YouTube
called Doe Deer Wonderland

00:00:17.235 --> 00:00:20.010
where I do doll restorations.

00:00:20.010 --> 00:00:23.880
This is a 1964 Ponytail Swirl Barbie.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.138
They had a limited run of about two years.

00:00:27.138 --> 00:00:29.297
They were basically the last dolls

00:00:29.297 --> 00:00:31.400
to represent '50s glamour.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:34.385
It makes them really
valuable to collectors.

00:00:34.385 --> 00:00:36.370
The hair is basically a mess.

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:37.860
It's frizzy.

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:40.910
The paint has basically chipped away.

00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:44.218
She has a bald spot, which
I'm going to be filling in.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.080
So, first I'm going to wash the doll

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.649
using dishwashing soap and a toothbrush.

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:11.030
Then I'm going to put fabric
conditioner in her hair

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:12.697
and comb it through.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:25.100
I use just a normal hairbrush,

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:28.160
and then I go over it with a fine comb

00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.410
once all the kinks are out.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:42.953
Next, I'm going to reroot
the doll using nylon hair.

00:01:47.550 --> 00:01:51.760
That's a specific tool for doll rerooting.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.323
So it's a needle that's been cut.

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:57.100
So I take the hank of hair,

00:01:57.100 --> 00:02:00.170
cut it to the length that I need,

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.870
then I put it around my finger,

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:05.136
and using the rerooting tool

00:02:05.136 --> 00:02:08.027
I just pick up small sections

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.503
and insert them into the doll's head.

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:20.013
Then I'm going to glue the hair in place.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.740
You glue it on the inside of the head

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:26.015
so that the hair doesn't come out

00:02:26.015 --> 00:02:29.006
when you brush it or work with it.

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:36.395
Then I boil the hair to keep
it down while I work on it.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:42.440
Boiling water basically
calms the hair fibers

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.770
and makes sure they lay in the position

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:46.603
that you want them to.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.128
I am giving her a haircut

00:02:59.128 --> 00:03:01.736
and putting her hair in rollers.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.880
The hair that you order
is not the correct length.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.870
You're always going to have some overhang,

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.100
so you're just going to want to cut that

00:03:10.100 --> 00:03:13.166
to match the doll's length.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:25.240
I just wrap the sections
with aluminum foil

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:27.990
and then roll them around the rollers.

00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:37.526
The rollers I made myself using Fimo clay.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:53.730
I go over her legs with a sandpaper block

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.813
to address the scratches.

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.890
As her face has become a bit green,

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.192
I'm going to counteract that

00:04:05.192 --> 00:04:08.241
using soft pastels with no primer.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:14.910
The vinyl is basically like human skin.

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:17.743
It absorbs anything you put on it.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.716
I go over it using

00:04:27.716 --> 00:04:30.700
a mixture of red and yellow and orange.

00:04:45.635 --> 00:04:49.862
Then I'm repainting her
face using acrylic paint.

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:55.038
The eyeliner is chipped,

00:04:55.038 --> 00:04:57.238
so there's pieces of it missing.

00:04:57.238 --> 00:04:59.840
The lips have faded to a white,

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:02.248
which is common for dolls like this.

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:11.004
I use a thin paintbrush so
I can detail all the makeup.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:19.170
These are specifically
made for detail work.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.573
Then I apply a semiglossy
varnish on the paint job.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:33.960
The varnish that I use,

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:37.120
it just helps preserve
the paint that I applied,

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.920
and it gives it a semiglossy finish.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:47.540
Her nails are faded,

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:49.181
and I need to go over them

00:05:49.181 --> 00:05:51.982
to make them decent again.

00:05:56.900 --> 00:05:58.900
The original hairstyle of the doll

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:02.590
was basically a low ponytail
with sideswept bangs

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:05.900
and a flip around the ponytail.

00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:07.531
I brush out her hair.

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:14.330
I am going to tie the hair in
the back in a low ponytail.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:27.196
Then I use hair mousse to
keep the hair in place.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:37.604
And I hide the elastic
band with a strand of hair.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.528
Then I set the curl around
my finger using hair mousse.

